  "interpretation": [
    "Public H2D payload and upload staging capacity equal rows*cols*8 for every measured pitch.",
    "For256x128/ld4224, public upload staging is262144 bytes versus the8617984-byte safe extent control (32.875x smaller requested upload storage/payload).",
    "Direct compact HIP2D copy+conversion often loses to the safe contiguous-extent control despite lower byte volume. Retain these losing cases; no general throughput speedup or routing promotion is claimed.",
    "Production already uses owned CPU gathering plus a contiguous transfer. These measurements do not justify replacing that policy with direct HIP2D copies.",
    "Other GPU/OS targets require their own qualification; the broad Linux/multi-GPU issues remain open."
  ]
